  ],
  "text": "A cyclone needs one thing to start. Ocean water warmer than twenty six degrees. Warm water evaporates. That much happens on any stove. That rising air cools, condenses, and dumps all its heat straight back out. The released heat pulls in even more air. Now the loop is feeding itself. But a feeding loop is still not a cyclone. It has no spin yet. The spin is borrowed from underneath. The whole planet is turning. Which is why no cyclone has ever formed on the equator. Nothing there to borrow. And it dies the moment it crosses land, because the fuel is behind it. So warm the ocean a little more and you do not get more storms. You get worse ones. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
